This project re-implements, in Rust, the behaviour of docx-to-pdf by Mohammad Alhaddar
(https://github.com/moalhaddar/docx-to-pdf), MIT License as stated in its README, version 2.1.0-13
(commit a692cfc286d3588b0c21456314cd605103810314). That repository is a git submodule at
upstream/docx-to-pdf, kept as reference and never built into this project.

Fonts in the image:
- Droid Arabic Kufi (upstream fonts/DroidKufi-*.ttf) — Apache License 2.0.
- Cantarell (upstream fonts/Cantarell-ExtraBold.otf) — SIL Open Font License 1.1.
Upstream's Brown Std (Lineto) and GE Dinar Two (Boutros International) are commercial, their licences
do not allow redistribution, and they are not distributed here.

LibreOffice is distributed by The Document Foundation under the Mozilla Public License 2.0; the image
installs it unmodified.

The corpus documents under tests/corpus/documents/third-party/ (tests/corpus/README.md) are copied
unmodified, each origin's licence text beside its documents:
- third-party/apache-poi/: test documents of Apache POI (https://github.com/apache/poi), Apache License
  2.0, with Apache POI's NOTICE.
Each folder's README.md names every document's path and git blob in its origin's repository. The five
under tests/corpus/documents/docx2pdf/ (harvest11, ramp_adv_1, sample1, sample2, size40) come from the
fixtures of the docx2pdf project by this project's author. The documents under
tests/corpus/documents/features/ are this project's own, written by generate.py beside them.
